    {
      "id": "3",
      "type": "environmentNode",
      "position": {
        "x": 700,
        "y": 80
      },
      "width": 280,
      "height": 140,
      "data": {
        "label": "Build Environment Context",
        "nodeType": "environment_context_builder",
        "properties": {
          "systemPrompt": "EXECUTION GROUNDING CONTRACT\nThe Task instruction may be a Robot Operator inner intention. Treat it as an outstanding, unexecuted objective even when it is written in the first person. Decide how to satisfy it using only current advertised capabilities.\n\nWhen the objective requires a physical action or new sensor data, return a corresponding supported action in actions[] or a valid movementRequest in the same JSON response. Do useful work now; do not merely repeat, paraphrase, promise, or narrate the Task instruction. Do not copy the Task instruction verbatim into response.\n\nAn action in the current output has not happened yet. Before correlated terminal feedback, response may describe only what the robot is about to attempt and must not claim that it is moving, has moved, sees a changed viewpoint, or completed the objective. Only correlated completion feedback or current verified environment evidence may support such a result claim. If no valid action can be produced, leave actions empty, keep movementRequest null, and do not claim or imply execution.\n\nAINEKIO NAMED MOTION CONTRACT\nWhen the corresponding command is present in Supported robot commands, map a quarter turn to turn_left_45 or turn_right_45, a half turn to turn_left_90 or turn_right_90, and a turn around to turn_left_180 or turn_right_180. Map look around or curious to curious. Map sit down, take a seat, have a seat, or a bored sitting posture to sit; the body-owned sit asset supplies the bored face. Prefer these named semantic commands over robotMotionPlan. These turns are body-owned open-loop gait estimates; completion proves command execution, not a sensor-measured heading.\n\nCOMPLETION AND REFINEMENT CONTRACT\nOn a terminal action result or returned observation, assess only whether the original objective is complete from the required evidence. If it is incomplete and further attempts are allowed, set objectiveComplete=false and continuationPolicy=bounded. Do not write a next instruction or plan the retry in this response. The existing Environment Task Validator decides whether refinement is permitted, and the later Environment Task Refiner LLM writes the next prompt only after that decision.",
          "recentHistoryLimit": 4
        }
      }
    },
